ory","decision_margin":-0.1875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: `@functools.cache def _source_kinds()`","AC2: 'a test that extends the compared tuple and asserts the derived set follows'","functools.cache retains the first return value; a later LAYER_ORDER extension is invisible without cache_clear"],"finding":"AC2 verifies that extending LAYER_ORDER flows through to the derived set, but the accessor is `@functools.cache`d. If the accessor has already been called in the interpreter (which AC1/AC1b tests do), the cache holds the pre-extension frozenset, so a naive 'extend the tuple and assert the set follows' test reads a stale value. The plan does not state how the AC2 test resets the cache (`_source_kinds.cache_clear()`) or otherwise avoids the cache, so the test as described is under-specified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3738824c97d6bc72","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2 / Approach (functools.cache accessor)","norm_id":"n8e66a8946976b3ac","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["AC2 test runs after any earlier test that called _source_kinds(), reads the cached stale frozenset, and either passes vacuously or fails confusingly"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In AC2, state that the test clears the accessor cache (`_source_kinds.cache_clear()`) after monkeypatching `config.LAYER_ORDER`, then asserts the derived frozenset reflects the extension.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justif